{# The one badge every sender status renders through — domain detail's Top
   Senders table and the Sender Inventory table both use it, so the two pages
   can never disagree about what a colour means again.

   The `title` carries SenderReviewState::meaning(), which is what turns an
   opaque amber pill into an answer to "does this require any action?". The
   legend and the KB article say the same thing at length; this is the version
   you get for free by hovering.

   Props:
     - state  (?SenderReviewState)  null = no known_sender row backs this row yet
#}
{% props state = null %}

{% if state is null %}
    <span class="badge badge-sm badge-ghost"
          title="No inventory entry for this sender yet — nothing to decide."
          data-testid="sender-status-badge"
          data-sender-state="untracked">Not tracked yet</span>
{% else %}
    <span class="badge badge-sm {{ state.badgeClass }}"
          title="{{ state.meaning }}"
          data-testid="sender-status-badge"
          data-sender-state="{{ state.value }}">{{ state.label }}</span>
{% endif %}
